    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The colonial state formed when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> government took over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">VOC</a>’s Asian possessions on 1 January 1800.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultivation-system">Cultivation System</a> of 1830 forced Javanese villages to grow export crops, making the colony highly profitable for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</li><li>Conquest of the outer islands by about 1910 created the borders that independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> inherited in 1949.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/multatuli">Eduard Douwes Dekker</a>, a former colonial official, attacked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultivation-system">Cultivation System</a> in the 1860 novel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/max-havelaar">Max Havelaar</a>, published under the pen name Multatuli.</p></aside>
    </section>

